yedek flanşlı somun M6 X 20 adet

50 adet M6 pul 

30 adet konumlandırma için M6 X 16mm X 30 adet


Metin metin 
bağımsız küresel iş Yeni hacim t32: *metin 
{
  hacim;
  tamlanmış := <d64>hacim + (@mimari - (<d64>hacim % @mimari));
  toplam := tamlanmış + @metin;
  Gelen := temiz(t8[toplam]);
  //c::stdio::printf('toplam: %d, hacim: %d, tamlanmış %d\n', toplam, hacim, tamlanmış); 
  sonuç = <*metin>Gelen;
  sonuç->hacim = <tam>tamlanmış;
  sonuç->boyut = 0;
  sonuç->_harfler = &Gelen[@metin];
  dön sonuç;
}

sanal iş _dboyut Sol *metin, Sağ *metin : tam 
{
  dön (seç Sol->hacim > Sağ->hacim: 
    hayır: Sol->hacim/<%Sol->hacim>(@mimari), 
    varsayılan: Sağ->hacim/<%Sol->hacim>(@mimari)); 
}

Metin metin 
bağımsız küresel 
iş Metinden Girdi *metin: *metin 
{
  Yeni := metin::Yeni(Girdi->boyut);
  _harfler := &Girdi->_harfler[0];
  geçir(&Yeni->_harfler[0], _harfler, Girdi->boyut); 
  Yeni->boyut = Girdi->boyut; 
  //stdio::printf('-?? %s, %s\n', Yeni->_harfler, _harfler);
  dön Yeni;
}

Ingredient	Amount	Notes
Chicken drumsticks	1,000 g	Protein & bone
Chicken heart	200 g	Taurine-rich muscle
Chicken liver	150 g	Vitamin-rich, limited for safety
Wet food	400 g	Smell/flavor for appeal
Quail eggs (w/shells)	4 (~200 g)	Calcium, protein, lecithin
Sweet potato or pumpkin	100 g	Gentle fiber (optional, rye alt)
Water	1,000 ml	Blending & hydration
Sardine oil (optional)	1 tsp	Omega-3 balance
Sunflower oil	1 tbsp	Omega-6 and energy


Homemade Kitten Food Recipe (Refined Version)

Chicken drumsticks: 1,000 g
Chicken heart: 200 g
Chicken liver: 150 g
Wet food (for smell/flavor appeal): 400 g
Quail eggs (with shells): 4 (~200 g)
Sweet potato or pumpkin (optional, as gentle fiber or rye alternative): 100 g
Water: 1,000 ml
Sardine oil (optional, for Omega-3): 1 tsp
Sunflower oil (for Omega-6 and energy): 1 tbsp

Preparation:

Boil the chicken drumsticks, hearts, and liver in 1 liter of water until fully cooked.
Remove solids and set aside.
Use the remaining broth to cook the sweet potato/pumpkin (or rye if you prefer).
While cooking, blend the broth with quail eggs (including crushed shells).
Combine everything (meat, wet food, blended mix, oils) in a large bowl.
Blend or mash to desired consistency (smooth for younger kittens).
Portion and refrigerate or freeze in small containers.


